      "message": "test(2d): port the offset engagement pins\n\nPort three engagement pins from PR #3439 onto main's Pass start law\n(level_rings / level_order). Each pin passes. Two PR pins are not ported:\none fails on main's law and one repeats main's existing coverage.\n\nKept:\n- outside_on_a_figure_eight_band_never_slots: Outside on a synthetic\n  figure-eight band never cuts wider than 1.5 stepovers over any 3 tool\n  radii of floor feed. Main has this law only in an ignored heavy app\n  test, so this pin gives default-suite coverage.\n- inside_on_the_band_clears_the_whole_band: Inside on the round-part\n  band leaves less than 0.5 mm2 of stock off the part wall, for both\n  climb directions.\n- auto_on_the_band_slots_so_the_measure_sees_a_slot: Auto (core first)\n  on the same band slots, so the width measure has a positive control.\n\nDropped:\n- outside_entries_after_the_first_land_in_cleared_stock: fails on main.\n  The later entries cut 332.88 mm2 of uncut stock. Main's law does not\n  lead a re-entry from cleared stock.\n- outside_on_a_split_band_never_slots: main's\n  outside_band_split_by_the_part_cuts_no_move_at_full_width already pins\n  the same Outside split-band law.\n\nRefs #3316\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
